<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 250 mln stg late help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 250 mln stg late help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with around 250 million stg of unspecified late assistance.  </p>
<p>			    EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    800 MLN    800 MLN    650 MLN    650 MLN</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    =	     33 MLN    366 MLN    616 MLN</p>
<p> BAND 1  BANK BILLS   =	     31 MLN*   297 MLN*    =</p>
<p> BAND 2  BANK BILLS   =		2 MLN*    36 MLN*    =</p>
<p> UNSPECIFIED ASSISTANCE					  250 MLN</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-15/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
